# --- Project data & outputs (large files + data sensitivity) ---
# Anchored to repo root so these DON'T also match ui/data/ (git can't re-include
# files inside an ignored dir, which would hide the small UI results below).
/data/
/outputs/
# ui/data: DENY everything, then re-include ONLY named municipal-aggregate artifacts.
#
# This used to whitelist by EXTENSION (`!ui/data/*.geojson`), which was a real hazard:
# the never-publish artifact is `outputs/catatumbo_2023_coca.geojson` — 2,065 plot-level
# 20 m polygons, targeting-usable — and it is a .geojson. Dropping any plot-level
# geojson into ui/data/ would have made it tracked, so the 75 m / municipal-aggregate
# rule was being enforced only by which directory today's code happens to write to.
# Enforce it here instead. Adding a NEW artifact must be a deliberate act.
ui/data/*
!ui/data/municipal_coca.csv
!ui/data/municipal_coca.geojson
!ui/data/municipal_coca_20[0-9][0-9].csv
!ui/data/municipal_coca_20[0-9][0-9].geojson
!ui/data/trend.json
# Per-year measured metrics the panel renders (A16 IoU + A17 rho, model and null),
# copied from outputs/metrics/baseline_ladder.jsonl so the UI quotes rows rather than
# hardcoded prose. Aggregates only — no geometry, no per-cell values.
!ui/data/metrics.json
*.tif
*.tiff
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
checkpoints/
# Re-include the blurred 75 m map-overlay COGs (after *.tif so this wins) — but by a
# CONSTRAINED pattern, not `!ui/data/*_cog.tif`. That glob would have tracked any COG at
# any resolution dropped in here, which is the same hazard as the extension whitelist
# above. A file must now be named density_<year>_cog.tif to be included, which cannot
# happen by accident.
!ui/data/density_20[0-9][0-9]_cog.tif
# The official census grid at the same 75 m / same footprint as the model layer, so the
# map can show "model vs census" as one comparison instead of asking for trust. Same
# constrained naming rule: it must be official_<year>_cog.tif. It carries no
# finer-than-1 km information — the source cells are constant-valued — and it is public
# data (datos.gov.co) to begin with.
!ui/data/official_20[0-9][0-9]_cog.tif
# True-colour Sentinel-2 for each year at the same 75 m, so the map has imagery that
# works without internet and that MATCHES the analysis year. Public Sentinel-2, coarser
# than its own native 10-20 m by the time it is written here.
!ui/data/rgb_20[0-9][0-9]_cog.tif

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Earth Engine / creds ---
*.json.key
.config/earthengine/
service-account*.json

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Agent config ---
# Was untracked AND un-ignored, so `git add -A` would have silently committed it.
# Ignored so that publishing it is a deliberate choice. The agent definitions are
# arguably a portfolio asset (they document the review workflow), so if you want them
# public do it on purpose: `git add -f .claude/`.
.claude/

# --- NEVER PUBLISHABLE, anywhere in the tree, regardless of every rule above ---
# Plot/field-level geometry is targeting-usable and is the one irreversible mistake this
# project could make. Listed LAST so these deny rules win against any re-include.
# (`outputs/` is already ignored; this is belt-and-braces for a file that gets moved.)
catatumbo_*_coca.geojson
*plot*.geojson
*parcel*.geojson
*field*.geojson
*footprint*.geojson
